; Tutorial 3.01: A First 3D Scene
;
; A 3D scene needs three things: a camera to look through, a light so that surfaces have shading, and something
; to look at. Everything in the 3D world is an "entity": cameras, lights, meshes, sprites and pivots. Each frame,
; RenderWorld draws what the cameras see, and Flip shows it.
;
; Directions: x points right, y points up and z points into the screen. The camera starts at (0, 0, 0) and looks
; along +z, so things need a positive z to be in front of it.
;
; Works on: the original Blitz3D and BlitzLLVM.

; Graphics3D is Graphics for 3D: width, height, depth (0 = best) and mode (2 = window).
Graphics3D 640, 480, 0, 2
AppTitle "Tutorial 3.01: A First 3D Scene"
SetBuffer BackBuffer()

Local camera = CreateCamera()
CameraClsColor camera, 30, 40, 70 ; The colour behind everything.

; A directional light shines in one direction, like the sun. RotateEntity points it: pitch 45 degrees down,
; turned 30 degrees around the vertical axis.
Local light = CreateLight()
RotateEntity light, 45, 30, 0

; AmbientLight lights every surface a little, so the sides away from the light are not black.
AmbientLight 60, 60, 80

; CreateCube makes a cube from -1 to 1 on every axis, so 2 units wide. PositionEntity moves it 5 units forward.
Local cube = CreateCube()
PositionEntity cube, 0, 0, 5
EntityColor cube, 255, 140, 40

; A sphere and a cylinder for company. The number is how many segments they are made of: more is rounder.
Local sphere = CreateSphere(24)
PositionEntity sphere, -3, 0, 7
EntityColor sphere, 80, 200, 255

Local cylinder = CreateCylinder(24)
PositionEntity cylinder, 3, 0, 7
EntityColor cylinder, 120, 255, 120

While Not KeyHit(1)
	; TurnEntity adds to the current rotation: pitch (around x), yaw (around y) and roll (around z), in degrees.
	TurnEntity cube, 0.5, 1, 0
	TurnEntity cylinder, 1, 0, 0

	RenderWorld ; Draws the 3D world into the back buffer.

	; 2D drawing still works after RenderWorld, on top of the 3D picture.
	Color 255, 255, 255
	Text 10, 10, "A camera, a light and three meshes. Escape quits."
	Text 10, 30, "Triangles drawn: " + TrisRendered()
	Flip
Wend
End
